description.narrative:
The goal of the project is to support economic transformation and sustainable and inclusive development in Vietnam. The overall objective is to support attaining this goal by contributing to data generation, economic analysis and modelling to improve the elaboration, monitoring, and evaluation of suitable economic policies.

Key results include the following:
•	Updated macro model with consistent 5-10-year growth projections to assess feasible growth targets for national planning;
•	New dynamic (GreenReform) CGE model and associated 2024 Social Accounting Matrix data set updating the 2019 SAM, where energy supply and use are integral elements to be able to analyse the impact of energy transition issues and policies. A modified dynamic GreenReform model to fit the Vietnamese economy will be developed and expanded to study the impact of different energy transition policy scenarios on industries, occupational groups, and income groups over time;
•	Six policy briefs linked to the six research studies, four training workshops, and 30 researchers at collaborating institutions trained in data development and model applications
